  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Crossovers in a circle with the ball going back",
  "description": "5–6 players line up on a circle, around the centre circle or a ring of cones about 10 metres across. Everyone skates the same way using crossovers. One player has the ball.\n\nThe ball carrier passes or drops the ball back to the player behind. The receiver carries it for a few strides and sends it on backwards to the next player. So the ball travels the opposite way to the skating.\n\nChange direction after a while so both legs get the work. Progression: two balls in the circle at once, or a first-time pass back without stopping the ball. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Deep knees and strong crossovers – the outside leg pushes under the body."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the speed even so the gaps between players stay the same."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look back over your shoulder before dropping the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The receiver keeps the stick on the ice and shows where the ball should go."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 2,
